# BUILD PROMPT — SCP Episode Intelligence Layer (Hybrid Architecture)
### Self-contained implementation brief. Assumes no prior knowledge of this project.

> **Placement.** Repo root as `COPILOT.md`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`,
> `CLAUDE.md`, or `AGENTS.md` — whichever your agent reads. Do not paste as a
> chat turn. Point the agent at a numbered section per task.
>
> **Fill every `[FILL]` in Section 1 before first use.** An agent that guesses
> your stack produces code you throw away.

---

# 0. READ THIS FIRST

You are building a **post-detection decision-support layer** for trade
surveillance at a regulated bank. Its output is evidence shown to a human
supervisor who carries personal regulatory accountability for the decision they
make. Every constraint in this document descends from that fact.

## 0.1 Three things to internalise

1. **A confident wrong answer is worse than no answer.** Degraded, partial,
   uncertain and inferred states must remain visibly so, all the way to the
   screen. Never fill a gap with a plausible default.
2. **Everything is evidence in a future audit.** A decision made today may be
   examined in seven years. Reproduce exactly what was shown, from what inputs,
   by which version — not an approximation.
3. **Conservative constraints here are load-bearing.** Several will look
   unnecessarily restrictive. One incorrect grouping presented to a supervisor
   destroys trust in the layer permanently. Do not relax one because it is
   inconvenient.

## 0.2 Your behavioural rules

- Do not resolve ambiguity silently. **Stop and ask.**
- Do not invent numeric values. See Section 2.
- Do not renegotiate anything marked SETTLED. If you disagree, implement it and
  record the disagreement in one labelled note. Do not build around it.
- Implement one section per task. Do not scaffold the whole system in one pass.
- Do not write to the CAL alert store under any circumstance, via any path.
- Do not give any agent a write tool.

