# 2. SETTLED / PLACEHOLDER / UNKNOWN

Consult before writing any constant.

## 2.1 SETTLED — implement exactly

- Read-only relationship to SCP and the CAL alert store
- Human-in-the-loop: no autonomous sign-off, RFI, or ownership move
- Append-only, bitemporal persistence throughout
- Three alert types: `CANCEL`, `AMEND`, `LATE`
- Episode linking is **already built**; consume its sealed payload, do not modify
- **Compute deterministically, interpret agentically** — no agent produces a
  number, a score, or a rank
- Agent layer is read-only, non-authoritative, and never a dependency of the queue
- Rule baseline score is mandatory and standalone; Isolation Forest is optional
  behind a flag
- Prioritisation sort terminates in `episode_id`
- Overrides are deterministic config evaluated outside any model
- Linkage rationale is templated from edges, never generated
- Every agent claim must trace to a tool result, validated programmatically
- `lineage_root_id` for history; `as_of_ts` for time cutoffs

## 2.2 PLACEHOLDER — read from config, never a literal

Fail loudly at startup if absent. Never default.

```
# Prioritisation
priority.urgency.critical_business_days      1
priority.urgency.near_business_days          3
priority.evidence.high_percentile            95
priority.evidence.elevated_percentile        85
priority.starvation_escalate_days            10
priority.b0_share_alarm_pct                  10
priority.default_deadline_business_days      5

# Signal store
signal.trader_baseline_window_days           365
signal.lateness_baseline_window_days         90
signal.recurrence_windows_days               [30, 90]
signal.peer_min_population                   30
signal.series_zscore_window_days             90

# Scoring
scoring.isolation_forest.enabled             false
scoring.isolation_forest.weight              0.4
scoring.rule_baseline.weight                 0.6
scoring.model_timeout_ms                     2000

# Agent layer
agent.model_version                          [FILL — pinned string]
agent.temperature                            0.0
agent.max_tool_calls_per_episode             12
agent.tool_timeout_ms                        5000
agent.total_budget_ms                        30000
agent.validation.reject_on_unsourced_number  true

# Queue
queue.promote_provisional_when_urgency_at    CRITICAL
```

Never derive a new constant from a placeholder. Needed value not on this list →
add to config and flag it.

## 2.3 UNKNOWN — business or compliance input required

Flag and stop if your work depends on one:

1. Review SLA per alert type (CANCEL, AMEND, LATE)
2. Firm materiality notional threshold for the B0 override
3. Retention period for signals, scores, narratives and traces
4. Entitlement policy for episodes spanning permission boundaries
5. Supervisor capacity for the inlier control sample
6. Whether Isolation Forest is admitted at all, or the score stays rule-only
7. **Model risk function's position on LLM-generated narrative in the review
   path** — critical path. If refused, the Analyst agent is removed and replaced
   with templated explanations; build Phase 1 accordingly.

---

# 3. CONTEXT AND ARCHITECTURE

## 3.1 The business problem

SCP, an existing rule engine, detects trade surveillance violations correctly.
Detection is not the problem. A single business action — a trader cancelling a
trade and rebooking its replacement — fires two or three independent SCP alerts
with nothing connecting them. Supervisors manually determine which alerts belong
together and reconstruct the business story before review can begin. There is no
consistent prioritisation against deadlines.

**This system removes reconstruction overhead and prioritises the queue. It does
not improve detection.**

## 3.2 Architecture

```
                    CAL alert store  (read-only source)
                            │
┌───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐
│  DETERMINISTIC SPINE      ▼   — system of record  │
│                                                   │
│   [A] Ingest and normalise                        │
│           │                                       │
│   [B] Episode linking       ALREADY BUILT         │
│           │                                       │
│   [C] Signal store  ───────────────────────────────────┐
│           │                                       │    │ read-only
│   [D] Score  (rules mandatory, IF optional)       │    │ typed tools
│           │                                       │    │
│   [E] Prioritised queue                           │    │
└───────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┘    │
            │           ┌─────────────────────────────────▼──┐
            │           │  [F] AGENT LAYER — read-only       │
            │           │      Case builder → Analyst        │
            │           │      Review assistant, Drafting    │
            │           └────────────────┬───────────────────┘
            ▼                            ▼
        ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
        │  [G] Supervisor — sole accountable     │
        │      Sign-off | RFI | Move | None      │
        └────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                         ▼
              [H] Outcomes and feedback
```

**Load-bearing property:** delete the agent layer entirely and the spine still
produces a ranked, defensible queue. The agent layer is additive, never a
dependency. Enforce this with an integration test, not a comment.

## 3.3 Stage isolation

Each stage reads only the sealed contract from its predecessor. The signal store
never reads the edge store. Scoring never reads raw alerts. Agents never read
any store directly — only through typed tools. Violating this produces two
computations of the same fact that drift apart, surfacing as an inexplicable
number rather than an error.

## 3.4 Provenance

This is a deliberate reduction of a larger prior design. Do not reintroduce cut
components.

| Component | Status | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Ingest, blocklist, trust registry | Kept | Highest-leverage control in the system |
| Episode linking | Kept, already built | Deterministic joins; an agent here would be slower, costlier, non-reproducible, hallucination-prone |
| Feature store platform | Reduced to signal store | Existed to feed five models; one model needs aggregates |
| Rule baseline | Kept, now primary | Fallback, benchmark, and the whole score in rule-only mode |
| Isolation Forest | Kept behind a flag | Real value on numeric outliers; flagged so governance can approve rule-only first |
| LOF | **Cut** | Recoverable from precomputed peer percentiles at a fraction of the cost |
| One-Class SVM | **Cut** | Redundant with IF, poor scaling |
| Autoencoder | **Cut** | Unjustified at ~40 features and three alert types |
| Prophet | **Cut** | Replaced by rolling z-score on counts |
| Ensemble consensus, cross-model percentile normalisation, frozen reference windows | **Cut** | Existed solely to combine five incomparable scores |
| Prioritisation logic | Kept unchanged | Pure policy; must stay deterministic |
| Templated linkage rationale | Kept unchanged | Must be exactly true, therefore not generated |
| SHAP | Kept only if IF enabled | Rule-only score explains itself |
| Narrative machinery | Replaced by Analyst agent | Where LLMs genuinely beat templates |
| Free-text handling | **New** | Prior design had none; strongest argument for the agent layer |

